====================================================================================
RECURSIVE-ACROSS-n: achievable gap fractions & height, per n
====================================================================================
    n                gap  #members  min M (=2nd val)  max c   height range  known?
    6         (1/6,2/11)         0             EMPTY      0             --     n/a
    7         (1/7,2/13)         1              5/33      5         17..17     YES
    8         (1/8,2/15)         1              3/23      3         18..18     YES
    9         (1/9,2/17)         0             EMPTY      0             --     n/a
   10        (1/10,2/19)         0             EMPTY      0             --     n/a
   11        (1/11,2/21)         0             EMPTY      0             --     n/a
   12        (1/12,2/23)         0             EMPTY      0             --     n/a
   13        (1/13,2/25)         0             EMPTY      0             --     n/a

  READING: max c = largest achievable numerator (Stern-Brocot depth).
  If max c CAPS (bounded) and DECREASES to 0 (empty) with n, and height
  stays ~linear, then a gap member's value denom q<=13c is bounded =>
  the residue-bridge census is FINITE = the height upper bound.
  (validation: n=7,8 must show known members found, not MISS.)
